{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1341772-new-legacy-urbanomancers","id":1341772,"title":"[New Legacy] Urbanomancers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-16T20:46:15-07:00","id":1341772,"title":"[New Legacy] Urbanomancers","content":"Note: The format for this Legacy is borrowed from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a>. I would especially like feedback on whether this is too much like House Of Ariadne, and on whether I should change it to Thyrsus-Fate.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Consider the idea of the city and how alive it feels. The vehicles in the streets like hemoglobin inside blood vessels. The commercial and residential buildings jutting from the concrete like skeletons of steel. The night clubs and musical concerts lighting up like dopamine in the brain. The city is alive not just metaphorically, but also metaphysically. The animistic spirits lurking beneath its skin are not just otherworldly parasites, but the key to making it beautiful and prosperous.<br /> <br /> Caught in the middle are those who built the city in the first place, and most of them don't realize the spiritual consequences of their daily choices. The city is not inherently a shelter, but a ravenous maw that devours people to keep its many engines running. It can no more be tamed than a Sleeper can survive inside the Shadow. This happens because the central spirit of each metropolis, known as a Cityfather, does not rule out of humane motivations.<br /> <br /> Enter the Urbanomancers, whose duty is to take on the mantle of and be an intermediate for the Cityfather. Like a neon and chrome rendition of the classical forest-keeper witch, Urbanomancers weave destinies and enforce oaths according to a mystical agenda only known to them. From the vagrants to the mayors, all are orchestrated through a sublime design for the perfect spiritual equilibrium. As they further embody their mantle, so too do they become one with their dominion.<br /> <br /> Origins<br /> Parentage: Acanthus, Free Council<br /> Nicknames: Street Urchins<br /> Background: Travelling performers, activists and various urban designers who wish to make their cities into ideal homes.<br /> Appearances: Urbanomancers have no standard dress code, since they come from all walks of life. However, they do have a tendency to keep an eye out for the latest fashions, and many adopt eclectic outfits which combine traits from multiple sub-cultures and tribes. Their Nimbi also manifest symbols of their favored types of spirit, often in the form of living tattoos.<br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 2, Streetwise 2, Occult 2 + Specialty for Spirits or equivalent field.<br /> Initiation: One must have a significant section or landmark of the city legally named after them as a mark of respect. After that, the initiate must enter the Shadow while accompanied by a mentor and have an audience with the Cityfather as a formality. The initiate becomes an Urbanomancer upon swearing fealty to this entity.<br /> <br /> Organization: Urbanomancers have little in the way of a formal hierarchy, but the members who have contributed the most to the safety and prosperity of their respective cities are considered the firsts among equals. They often form sub-divisions based on complementary talents both mundane and magical, with a focus on improving the more destitute and overlooked sections of their cities. An uniting feature of the Legacy is a holistic engagement with the city's affairs and issues, which lends itself to extensive networking and information gathering. Urbanomancers also make frequent use of spirits as proxies and assistants, which gives them clearer insight into the city and allows them to strategically influence Resonances. Last but not least, they hold an annual gathering inside a Place That Isn't inside the Shadow which reflects the zeitgeist's idealized metropolis.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Spirit<br /> Yantras: Symbols of your favored types of urban spirits (+1 or +2 if especially prominent), acting in accordance with spiritual omens (+1 or +2 if this causes a Condition), succeeding on a Streetwise roll relevant to the spell (+2), items or locations touched by the Numina or Influences of the Cityfather (+2)<br /> Oblations: Explaining and enforcing oaths and traditions, selective and systematic cultivation of Resonances, exploring the Shadow<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> First: Concrete Jungle<br /> Prerequisite: Initiation<br /> The Urbanomancer knows the abilities and natures of the city's spiritual residents. This Attainment works like Know Spirit, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> Optional: Fate 1<br /> The Urbanomancer is likewise familiar with the relationships between human residents and the city. This Attainment works like Interconnections, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> Second: Face Of The Neighborhood<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 2, either Streetwise 3 or Occult 3<br /> The Urbanomancer wields the authority of the Cityfather and forbids hostile spirits from attacking him. This Attainment works like Ephemeral Shield, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Fate 2<br /> The Urbanomancer is a pivotal figure of good fortune for his community and must exemplify such prosperity in his own endeavors no matter where he goes. This Attainment works like Warding Gesture, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> Third: The Streets Remember<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 3, both Streetwise 3 and Occult 3<br /> The Urbanomancer can ask spirits what they known about past events in the city. This works like Reverberations (shown below), with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, gaining additional information and recalling events from weeks ago.<br /> Optional: Fate 3<br /> The Urbanomancer cannot be fooled by oathbreakers that dishonor the city. This Attainment works like Oaths Fulfilled, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Area).<br /> <br /> Reverberations (Spirit \u25cf)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Empathy, Occult<br /> Withstand: Rank<br /> The Mage peers into the memories of the spirit, allowing him to ask a number of yes or no questions related to the spirit's purview equal to Potency. The only limitation is that the spirit cannot recall information from more than [Potency] days ago.<br /> +1 Reach: The spirit recalls additional information. For instance: a gun spirit not only says if it was used in a murder, but also gives a description of the murderer and victim.<br /> +1 Reach: The spirit can recall information from [Potency] weeks ago.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Harmony Between Tribes<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 4, Streetwise 4 and Occult 3, or Streetwise 3 and Occult 4<br /> The Urbanomancer controls legions of spirits to act as his vassals and enact his sublime design for the city. This Attainment works like Command Spirit, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Subjects).<br /> Optional: Fate 4<br /> The Urbanomancer establishes oaths between the citizens so as to enforce spiritual equilibrium. This Attainment works like Sworn Oaths, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Subjects).<br /> <br /> Fifth: Heart Of The Metropolis<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 5, both Streetwise 4 and Occult 4<br /> The Urbanomancer forms a domain for himself inside the Shadow which represents his metaphysical synonymy with the city. This Attainment works like Spirit Manse, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Fate 5<br /> The Urbanomancer fuses his destiny with that of the city. This Attainment works like Shared Fate, which is cast a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Scale (Area), Advanced Duration and making the link work in one direction only. Essentially, any harm done to the Urbanomancer is reflected to his Spirit Manse and thus sends ripples throughout the entire Shadow of the metropolis.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:48:18-07:00","id":1341773,"title":"","content":"By the way, if an Urbanomancer wants to swear fealty to another Cityfather for whatever reason, they can do that. But I have not decided what that might entail. I shall reserve this post for explaining that once it comes to my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T16:58:15-07:00","id":1341965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1341772-new-legacy-urbanomancers#post1341772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: The format for this Legacy is borrowed from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that guy, he's a jerk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would especially like feedback on whether this is too much like House Of Ariadne, and on whether I should change it to Thyrsus-Fate. </div> </div> </div>My initial thought is &quot;probably yes&quot; to both, but let's dive in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consider the idea of the city and how alive it feels. The vehicles in the streets like hemoglobin inside blood vessels. The commercial and residential buildings jutting from the concrete like skeletons of steel. The night clubs and musical concerts lighting up like dopamine in the brain. The city is alive not just metaphorically, but also metaphysically. The animistic spirits lurking beneath its skin are not just otherworldly parasites, but the key to making it beautiful and prosperous. </div> </div> </div>This is super very Thyrsus. Even an Acanthus with Life and Spirit would not naturally think in terms of ecosystems and a city being <i>alive</i> as their primary way of interfacing with reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Caught in the middle are those who built the city in the first place, and most of them don't realize the spiritual consequences of their daily choices. The city is not inherently a shelter, but a ravenous maw that devours people to keep its many engines running. It can no more be tamed than a Sleeper can survive inside the Shadow. This happens because the central spirit of each metropolis, known as a Cityfather, does not rule out of humane motivations. </div> </div> </div>There are certainly ways to flavor this to be more Acanthus and less Thyrsus, but again this screams &quot;Thyrsus&quot; at a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Enter the Urbanomancers, whose duty is to take on the mantle of and be an intermediate for the Cityfather. Like a neon and chrome rendition of the classical forest-keeper witch, Urbanomancers weave destinies and enforce oaths according to a mystical agenda only known to them. From the vagrants to the mayors, all are orchestrated through a sublime design for the perfect spiritual equilibrium. As they further embody their mantle, so too do they become one with their dominion. </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> 1) I hate the name because I'm a pedant and &quot;-mancer&quot; refers to divination, not diplomacy or magic in general.<br /> 2) I could see an Acanthus legacy revolving around being an intermediary, but these sound more like envoys or supplicants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Origins<br /> Parentage: Acanthus, Free Council<br /> Nicknames: Street Urchins<br /> Background: Travelling performers, activists and various urban designers who wish to make their cities into ideal homes.<br /> Appearances: Urbanomancers have no standard dress code, since they come from all walks of life. However, they do have a tendency to keep an eye out for the latest fashions, and many adopt eclectic outfits which combine traits from multiple sub-cultures and tribes. Their Nimbi also manifest symbols of their favored types of spirit, often in the form of living tattoos. </div> </div> </div>The plural of &quot;nimbus&quot; is &quot;nimbuses.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 2, Streetwise 2, Occult 2 + Specialty for Spirits or equivalent field.<br /> Initiation: One must have a significant section or landmark of the city legally named after them as a mark of respect. After that, the initiate must enter the Shadow while accompanied by a mentor and have an audience with the Cityfather as a formality. The initiate becomes an Urbanomancer upon swearing fealty to this entity. </div> </div> </div>The initiation requirement of having a &quot;significant section or landmark&quot; named after them is extremely steep. This normally happens posthumously to icons and heroes, even when it isn't posthumous it's still something you'd expect at the end of a story not as a backstory and probably not something that is accomplished by the time a new and inexperienced character is ready to join a legacy.<br /> <br /> I think swearing an oath to the Cityfather is probably enough of an initiation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Organization: Urbanomancers have little in the way of a formal hierarchy, but the members who have contributed the most to the safety and prosperity of their respective cities are considered the firsts among equals. They often form sub-divisions based on complementary talents both mundane and magical, with a focus on improving the more destitute and overlooked sections of their cities. An uniting feature of the Legacy is a holistic engagement with the city's affairs and issues, which lends itself to extensive networking and information gathering. Urbanomancers also make frequent use of spirits as proxies and assistants, which gives them clearer insight into the city and allows them to strategically influence Resonances. Last but not least, they hold an annual gathering inside a Place That Isn't inside the Shadow which reflects the zeitgeist's idealized metropolis. </div> </div> </div>&quot;A<s>n</s> uniting&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Spirit<br /> Yantras: Symbols of your favored types of urban spirits (+1 or +2 if especially prominent), acting in accordance with spiritual omens (+1 or +2 if this causes a Condition), succeeding on a Streetwise roll relevant to the spell (+2), items or locations touched by the Numina or Influences of the Cityfather (+2)<br /> Oblations: Explaining and enforcing oaths and traditions, selective and systematic cultivation of Resonances, exploring the Shadow </div> </div> </div>&quot;Acting in accordance with spiritual omens&quot; should grant a +2 on a detrimental condition.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised &quot;city beautification&quot; and &quot;public works projects&quot; aren't oblations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments<br /> First: Concrete Jungle<br /> Prerequisite: Initiation<br /> The Urbanomancer knows the abilities and natures of the city's spiritual residents. This Attainment works like Know Spirit, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> Optional: Fate 1<br /> The Urbanomancer is likewise familiar with the relationships between human residents and the city. This Attainment works like Interconnections, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. </div> </div> </div><i>Know Spirit</i> requires you to be able to touch the Spirit. Both <i>Know Spirit</i> and <i>Interconnections</i> are Withstood, making them weak early attainments (they will almost always be withstood with only two potency).<br /> <br /> I like <i>Exorcist's Eye</i>, because while it has overlap with the Spirit 2 attainment it doesn't require the use of Active Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Fate doesn't really have any great options for 1 dot attainments except for <i>Serendipity</i>, luckily <i>Serendipity</i> can be flavored as the Mage asking the Cityfather for advice, so it can fit the flavor of the Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: Face Of The Neighborhood<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 2, either Streetwise 3 or Occult 3<br /> The Urbanomancer wields the authority of the Cityfather and forbids hostile spirits from attacking him. This Attainment works like Ephemeral Shield, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Fate 2<br /> The Urbanomancer is a pivotal figure of good fortune for his community and must exemplify such prosperity in his own endeavors no matter where he goes. This Attainment works like Warding Gesture, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. </div> </div> </div>Of note, <i>Ephemeral Shield</i> does not actually prevent hostile spirits from attacking the subject physically without the additional reach option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third: The Streets Remember<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 3, both Streetwise 3 and Occult 3<br /> The Urbanomancer can ask spirits what they known about past events in the city. This works like Reverberations (shown below), with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, gaining additional information and recalling events from weeks ago.<br /> Optional: Fate 3<br /> The Urbanomancer cannot be fooled by oathbreakers that dishonor the city. This Attainment works like Oaths Fulfilled, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Area). </div> </div> </div>I don't see how <i>Oaths Fulfilled </i>really does anything with the given reach options that isn't already functionally covered by <i>Interconnections</i> as the first attainment. I could see making it Advanced Duration, Advanced Scale (Area), and &quot;receives a brief vision of the subject when the oath is fulfilled&quot; and then they go around setting up detection zones in relevant locations with the trigger &quot;does something to harm the city.&quot; This would let the Mage know when a city official embezzles or a corrupt cop does something wrong within the detection zone and would give the Mage knowledge of the offender.<br /> <br /> For my issues with <i>Reverberations</i> I just replied to the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reverberations (Spirit \u25cf)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Empathy, Occult<br /> Withstand: Rank<br /> The Mage peers into the memories of the spirit, allowing him to ask a number of yes or no questions related to the spirit's purview equal to Potency. The only limitation is that the spirit cannot recall information from more than [Potency] days ago.<br /> +1 Reach: The spirit recalls additional information. For instance: a gun spirit not only says if it was used in a murder, but also gives a description of the murderer and victim.<br /> +1 Reach: The spirit can recall information from [Potency] weeks ago. </div> </div> </div>There is no reason to limit the Spirit on the basis of this spell, the Spirit is an independent entity and should have a memory appropriate to its nature. Frankly, the best model for this spell is probably the Mind 3 spell <i>Read the Depths</i>, you could probably just copy the spell whole cloth replacing the Withstand: Resolve with Withstand: Rank and assigning the Reach to Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Withstand&quot; comes before &quot;Suggested Rote Skills.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth: Harmony Between Tribes<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 4, Streetwise 4 and Occult 3, or Streetwise 3 and Occult 4<br /> The Urbanomancer controls legions of spirits to act as his vassals and enact his sublime design for the city. This Attainment works like Command Spirit, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Subjects).<br /> Optional: Fate 4<br /> The Urbanomancer establishes oaths between the citizens so as to enforce spiritual equilibrium. This Attainment works like Sworn Oaths, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale (Subjects). </div> </div> </div>I think <i>Sworn Oaths</i> with Instant Casting and Advanced Duration is a better fit, that way the Mage can hold politicians to campaign promises and things of that nature, otherwise you need a bunch of people and/or spirits willing to sit there and all swear an oath together.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fifth: Heart Of The Metropolis<br /> Prerequisite: Spirit 5, both Streetwise 4 and Occult 4<br /> The Urbanomancer forms a domain for himself inside the Shadow which represents his metaphysical synonymy with the city. This Attainment works like Spirit Manse, which is cast as a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Fate 5<br /> The Urbanomancer fuses his destiny with that of the city. This Attainment works like Shared Fate, which is cast a Ritual and with Reach assigned to Advanced Scale (Area), Advanced Duration and making the link work in one direction only. Essentially, any harm done to the Urbanomancer is reflected to his Spirit Manse and thus sends ripples throughout the entire Shadow of the metropolis.[/SPOILER] </div> </div> </div>The <i>Spirit Manse</i> one is... fine? I guess. A little boring, but functional.<br /> <br /> The Fate one just seems bad, why would the protectors of the city want to hurt the city? Taking on the city's injuries to themselves maybe, but reflecting their injuries onto the city seems counterproductive.<br /> <br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________<br /> <br /> <br /> My final thoughts:<ul><li>There's nothing &quot;-mancer&quot; about this particular Legacy.</li> <li>The flavor is much more Thyrsus than Acanthus.</li> <li>If left as an Acanthus legacy there's definitely some thematic overlap between this legacy and the Ariadne, though not much mechanical overlap.</li> <li>Some of the attainments need work.</li> <li>I'd expand on this legacy being heralds and speakers for the Cityfather; they speak for the city because the city cannot speak directly to the inhabitants.</li> <li>To the previous point, Space or Mind might make more sense than Fate as the ruling Arcanum.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 10-18-2019, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T12:31:20-07:00","id":1342391,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Urbanomancers from Unknown Armies ? They have some cool powers and flavor, perhaps some of it can be useful for this Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}